        action recallIndexesBodiesAndRanksProperly;
        verification recallIndexesBodiesAndRanksProperlyDoD : Test { :>> id = "1396c570-9960-4831-8302-281016048e6d"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "DONE MEANS: recall seeds on the BODY fields it already reads, and ranks by a graded weight rather than a binary vote. Measured by the panel: seeds_for matches name, title and Alias term ONLY (knowledge.rs seeds_for), so decision/description/rationale/actionText/consequences are loaded and used only to PRINT the top rows - a prompt about provenance contributed zero seeds because the word lives in bodies and in no name or title. And agreement reaches max 1 in 43 of 50 bench cases, so the primary sort key is constant and the production ranker degenerates to (hops, name) - alphabetical - which is the exact failure agreement was introduced to fix. Cause is structural: MAX_PROMPT_WORDS caps votes at 3 and the rarity ceiling deletes the mid-frequency words most likely to co-occur. BM25 measured on the SAME name+title fields scores 37/50 (74%) at hit@20 against the shipped 24/50 (48%), with a field ceiling of 44/50. VERIFY: bodies are indexed for seeding; scoring is IDF-weighted with length normalisation (BM25) replacing MAX_PROMPT_WORDS + the rarity ceiling + the 55-word list + the agreement key, keeping the identifier override; the corrected harness shows no regression against the shipped 24/50."; }
