        action dcAcceptanceBindsToTheText;
        verification dcAcceptanceBindsToTheTextDoD : Test { :>> id = "b0cfb1a7-5230-45a4-877e-3f73fa2ffe2d"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "DONE MEANS: an accepted Decision whose text changed after its acceptance computes as NOT accepted, rather than as accepted. Landscape finding (agent-corral-landscape-2026-09-02, from mcp-scan's rug-pull class and PAuth's operand binding): acceptance today binds to a commit SHA (govern.rs acceptance_judged_against) and nothing compares the Decision body at that SHA with the body at HEAD - so the text a human signed and the text the tree carries can diverge silently, which is the same failure keel already refuses for evidence (judgedAgainst must resolve) and for confirmations (the quote receipt). DO: a guard - acceptance-binds-to-text - that, for every Decision carrying an acceptance, reads the decision/rationale/consequences fields at the acceptance's judgedAgainst SHA via git and at HEAD, and reports a violation when they differ; the acceptance is then reported by orient as suspect, exactly as drifted evidence is. Grandfather nothing: measure first, and if any accepted Decision already drifted, that is a finding to record, not a case to allowlist. VERIFY: a fixture with an accepted Decision, edit its decision field, guard goes red naming the Decision and both SHAs; revert, green; the live repo measured and its number stated."; }
