        action dcProvenanceAsRefs;
        verification dcProvenanceAsRefsDoD : Test { :>> id = "0d8000da-0814-60da-9b3e-0000003000da"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::demo; :>> procedureText = "Panel finding (e). `createdBy`, `owner` and `judgedBy` are `String` while `part def Actor` exists and is instantiated, so ~3000 attestation records carry an actor NAME that no viewer can navigate — you cannot select an actor and see what they authored or attested. This is the only trace that survives a provenance audit and it is the one with no edge, which matters directly under D0129, where provenance is never defaulted and an AI must never be able to pass as a human. NO PARSER GAP EXCUSES IT: all three fields are single-valued, and the single-valued `ref` assignment is confirmed portable in BOTH toolchains — the multi-valued sequence gap that sysmlv2-syntax-notes.md blames does not apply. DO: `ref createdBy : Actor[0..1];`, `ref owner : Actor;`, `ref judgedBy : Actor;`, with `ci` modelled as a registered tool Actor rather than a magic string. D0067 gated migration with a committed transform and reconciled control totals; the `actors` guard must see the identical actor set before and after, proven by capturing its output on both sides. VERIFY: an unregistered actor still FAILS the actors guard; confirmation-authenticity still distinguishes human from AI; every judgedBy resolves to a registered Actor; counts reconcile exactly; green at each phase."; }
        action dcUntrustedTaintClosure;
        verification dcUntrustedTaintClosureDoD : Test { :>> id = "a6aef919-39fe-4327-ad49-97f709c44952"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "DONE MEANS: nothing transitively derived from an untrusted utterance reaches a privileged sink without the label travelling with it. Landscape finding (CaMeL capability labels): guard 56 untrusted-routing enforces the ROUTING of an untrusted Statement - plan only, propose a Decision, a human accepts. It does not follow the label through derivation: a UserStory derived from an untrusted Statement, a Need derived from that story, a task chartered by that Need - three hops and the label is gone, and the task builds. DO: compute the taint closure over #DerivedFrom / #CharteredBy / #Resolves edges from every Statement with sourceTrust = untrusted, and refuse (violation) when a tainted item is an accepted Decision, a #SafetyChange or #ProspectiveChange, a guard or contract edit, or a task whose sprint has an Implement gate passing - unless the path crosses a human acceptance, which is the point at which trust is conferred. VERIFY: a fixture chain Statement(untrusted) -> UserStory -> Need -> task with a passing Implement gate goes red naming the path; the same chain with an accepted Decision between Need and task is green; the live repo measured against the 14 untrusted statements it holds."; }
