        verification dcConsentIsScopedAndExpiresDoD : Test { :>> id = "bd14f8d9-aaab-47ce-aba7-0668d8b69de4"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::demo; :>> procedureText = "DONE MEANS: a FORK Decision is written and put to the human on whether standing consent (D0207) binds to the revision of the rule it was granted under and whether it expires. Landscape finding: every in-path product the spike examined treats a standing, revision-unbound, non-expiring grant as the artifact to distrust - Entra Agent ID time-bounds grants and re-opens approval on extension, CapLease shows single-use tokens still replay under agent retry unless durable state records the confirmation event and remaining budget, and the untrusted commenter on the override thread asked exactly this. MEASURED: an auto-acceptance names D0207 and quotes the standing words but records neither the commit of the D0207 file nor the guard-set revision at acceptance (decision-issue.yml auto-accept step). OPTIONS, each costed: (a) keep as is and state why - the override thread is the escape valve and the human chose it; (b) stamp the D0207 revision and guard count on every auto-acceptance so a later change to the rule makes earlier consents visibly pre-revision (cheap, informational); (c) bind consent to the revision - a change to D0207 or a weakening of the guard set lapses standing consent until re-granted, so every auto-accept after it is refused until the human re-consents (a control, with a cost in interruptions); (d) add an expiry the human sets. VERIFY: the proposal passes judgment-request-quality (guard 48) - short name, rationale, per-option cost, a --research statement citing the knowledge record - and is surfaced to the human through decision-surfacing before the turn ends."; }
