        action dcComputedViewsRenderAndLink;
        verification dcComputedViewsRenderAndLinkDoD : Test { :>> id = "ac2548a5-545b-44db-ae42-0ee2e5ea7e1f"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Resolves issue286, reported by the human: tools give a vanilla json payload, needs to be displayed properly and link to items properly and dynamically. The generic viewpoint panel rendered every unbespoke view as pre JSON.stringify - a payload the reader parses by eye, with item names as dead text - while itemLink, openItem and the /api/item/:name endpoint had existed all along. The console had a working navigation mechanism the generic panel did not use. DO: a generic renderer that puts scalars in a headline row, arrays of objects in tables with the union of their keys as columns, and turns anything shaped like a keel item name into a live link that openItem resolves against the model AT CLICK TIME, so a view gains working links with no per-view code; keep the raw payload available in a collapsed details block, because a rendered table is a READING of the data and the reader must be able to check it against what the server sent. VERIFY: a computed view renders as tables rather than a JSON blob; an item name in it opens that item; a name that is not an item says so rather than failing silently; the raw payload is still reachable."; }
