        verification retireTheConfidenceProseDoD : Test { :>> id = "dc7a47d6-bd8f-43dd-93eb-7b9688d73166"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "DONE MEANS: no surface claims a confidence gate that does not exist. confident() discards every parameter and returns seed_count > 0, so the only prompts silenced are those with no informative token - which prompt_tokens already rejects upstream. Yet three surfaces still assert a gate: the main.rs doc comment listing kill switch 3 ('a LOW-confidence prompt is not injected at all. Silence is the default whenever recall cannot show it has found the right thing'), a PASSING DoD (kgPromptPathInjects: 'Injection is gated on a CONFIDENCE verdict - silence beats noise'), and the printed HIGH/LOW label itself, where LOW is unreachable whenever any row is shown so the label carries no information while reading as if it does - the panel observed 'confidence HIGH' on a payload that was 14 of 17 rows off-topic. Also in scope, same class: three wrong or contradictory numbers in my own comments - the ceiling described as '~60' when it computes to 68, 'gate (5,736)' at one line and '5,806' at another, and the ceiling credited with dropping `gate` when the five-character length rule drops it first and it never reaches the frequency check. VERIFY: the doc comment, the DoD text and the label are corrected or removed together; a test pins that no surface names a gate the code does not implement."; }
