        action dcNoOpInvarianceControl;
        verification dcNoOpInvarianceControlDoD : Test { :>> id = "664ec1c7-c38a-4326-9402-6ae60afe61ce"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Resolves issue310. THE CONTROL: no-op invariance - a command told to make a change that is already TRUE must leave the file byte-identical. Chosen because it needs no inventory of human-editable facts and cannot be defeated by refactoring: regeneration is lossless only when the model can represent every byte present, so a no-op that alters the file proves a fact the writer cannot round-trip. It would have failed on issue293 the day it shipped. VERIFY: keel-cli/tests/no_op_writes_lose_nothing.rs 7/7 - no-op activate, repeated deactivate, no-op viewpoint switch, a hand-added user key surviving sync-claude (the .claude preservation claim asserted in a doc comment and never tested), a second sync being inert, a hand-added comment surviving migrate's pin re-stamp, and a COVERAGE FLOOR failing when the source grows a whole-file write to a tracked surface no case exercises. The floor must be shown to have found something REAL: it found engine-version.toml (migrate re-stamped from a template - the same class, fixed here) and named adoption-profile.toml and keel-wrapper.toml scaffold-only with the reason in the source."; }
