        action dcAttestationBindsToDevice;
        verification dcAttestationBindsToDeviceDoD : Test { :>> id = "9199c135-40b6-45a8-b918-0bf6a1389f73"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Charters D0201 OPTION B, which the human CHOSE on 2026-08-23 (d0201Accept: 'deck-tap signature binding: device HMAC on taps, read-back ratification for chat approvals', bound to a single uncontradicted tap, uid 553d2b58) and which no tracked work ever carried - found by the rigor audit seven days later, because the decision-scaffolding warning naming it stood unread behind 61 undischargeable warnings. DO: a deck tap carries a device-scoped HMAC so a recorded human attestation is bound to the device that made it, not merely asserted by the server that received it; a chat-sourced approval is ratified by READ-BACK before it becomes a method=confirmation result. VERIFY BOTH DIRECTIONS: a tap with a valid device HMAC records and one with an absent or wrong HMAC is REFUSED with nothing written; a chat approval that is not read back does not become a confirmation. THE SCOPE BOUNDARY: this binds a tap to a DEVICE, not to a person's identity - say so in the record, since an attestation that overclaims what it proves is worse than one that claims less."; }
