        action dcMigrationRollsBack;
        verification dcMigrationRollsBackDoD : Test { :>> id = "a0d760ef-bae1-4d80-a16c-d8f8568c9891"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Charters D0252's unbuilt clause: a migration that cannot finish ROLLS BACK. migrate.rs contains no rollback today (grep: zero occurrences), so a migration that fails partway leaves a project in a state neither vintage - and D0067 already names a partially migrated project that reports success as the most expensive possible outcome. The existing guarantee is weaker than the Decision claims: blockers abort BEFORE anything is written, which covers refusal but not a mid-apply failure (a disk error, a permission denial, an interrupted run). DO: apply the plan so that a failure at any step restores the tree to its pre-migration state. VERIFY: a migration interrupted mid-apply leaves the tree byte-identical to its pre-run state, held by a fault-injected test - a rollback that has never been observed to run is a claim, not a mechanism (the arming discipline, D0253)."; }
