        action dcBatchedGovernanceIndex;
        verification dcBatchedGovernanceIndexDoD : Test { :>> id = "16960044-e826-4a27-96bd-7ced2939ef98"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Resolves issue316. The governance traversal is BATCHED so the antiquated-data question can actually be asked. Before: reprocess-candidates did not finish - 240 seconds, exit 124, zero bytes, measured twice - because each item cost a pickaxe search over full history plus a merge-base per process-change Decision (a single item timed at ~15s, so 501 stories is roughly two hours). DO: one rev-list builds the child map and forward-reachability sets per marker commit, so is_ancestor is a set lookup; one git log -p over .tracking/delivery maps every name to its introducing commit; charter edges come from the WORKING TREE, decision-introduction commits and process-def touches from one log each. VERIFY BOTH HALVES, because speed alone proves nothing: (1) the corpus lens EXITS 0, returns its answer and is NON-VACUOUS - an empty result on a corpus that has safety changes and items predating them would be a mis-aimed lens, not a clean bill of health; (2) the batched path is BYTE-IDENTICAL to the per-item resolver on three real corpus items chosen across vintages, since one item could agree by luck. Held by batched_governance_agrees.rs."; }
