        action dcStpaDiagramInTheBinary;
        verification dcStpaDiagramInTheBinaryDoD : Test { :>> id = "412b68fb-c317-4e24-9933-f5a8e600ee10"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "DONE MEANS: keel render control-structure --mode graph (or keel show control-structure --svg) draws the STPA diagram in the binary, byte-for-byte equivalent to .engine/tools/stpa_diagram.py on the same JSON, and the Python tool is deleted in the same commit. D0221: deterministic logic goes in the binary, I/O stays a thin step; a renderer in Python under .engine/tools is the sanctioned interim only. The five properties (D0285) become unit tests on the layout: no two segments collinear; every edge has a label naming what passes; every vertical/horizontal crossing carries a hop; controllers never overlap a drop lane; feedback enters bottom-right and control leaves bottom-left. VERIFY: the tests; the console serves the SVG at the safety viewpoint; the skill and process text name the binary command and no longer the tool (doc-sync in the same commit); tool-reference stays green after the deletion."; }
        action dcEmptyIsNothingDone;
        verification dcEmptyIsNothingDoneDoD : Test { :>> id = "a89c6783-deb6-4621-985b-c683c075d4c9"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "DONE MEANS: no ratio or readiness verdict keel computes reads 100 percent or READY over an empty population. MEASURED before: a fresh scaffold's report assurance showed three 100 percent cards and READY; tier-satisfaction pct 100 per empty tier; assured ready true. DO: every pct helper returns 0 on an empty denominator; a missing tier is 0; readiness requires governed > 0 and the verdict is three-valued (NOTHING TO ASSURE / READY / NOT READY); an empty tone on ratio cards; the pinned 'vacuously complete' test inverted with its reason; a source-scan test that fails the build on any division falling back to 100. VERIFY: the scaffold sweep across every lens and report finds no 100, READY or PASS-over-nothing; this repository's own verdicts are unchanged (NOT READY, 379 governed); the scan test catches a planted map_or(100."; }
