        // ---- then, in priority order: the accepted D0129/D0128 programme ----
        action dcStaleKernelInstanceGate;
        verification dcStaleKernelInstanceGateDoD : Test { :>> id = "0d5e0010-0812-4e10-9b3e-00000000e010"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Resolves issue081. The pre-commit hook runs the KERNEL validator .engine/tools/validate/validate_instances.py, which validates each .engine instance file IN ISOLATION — so any cross-file reference fails to resolve. It therefore ALREADY FAILS 11 COMMITTED decision files (0114, 0116-0125) on `Couldn't resolve reference to Element 'dNNNN'` / 'nViewerX' / Type 'DerivedFrom', which means the only way those commits landed was SKIP_VALIDATE=1 — the gate is routinely bypassed, which is the exact dynamic issue076 warns about (a gate contributors learn to bypass is defeated everywhere at once). Meanwhile `keel check-engine` (D0112 phase 2, kernel-free) resolves references ACROSS files and passes clean, so the Rust path is both correct and stricter here. NOTE the kernel ALSO cannot resolve `DerivedFrom` — independent confirmation of issue077 (the marker is undeclared). DO: retire validate_instances.py from the blocking hook path in favour of `keel check-engine` (the D0112 phase-3 direction), or fix it to register all instance packages before validating (the same two-pass shape as issue079). Either way the gate must stop failing files that are correct. This changes what gates a commit, so it is a CHANGE (§3a) needing a Decision + acceptance. VERIFY: no committed .engine file fails the enforced instance gate; the gate needs no routine bypass; check-engine still catches a genuine unresolved reference (negative test); clippy + cargo test + keel validate + guard green."; }
