        action dcParserReadSpecialize;
        verification dcParserReadSpecializeDoD : Test { :>> id = "0d800075-0814-6075-9b3e-000000300075"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Reads the `:>` SPECIALIZATION clause — construct 1 of dcParserReadBase, ranked first because `:>` is the derivation form D0140 names as the only valid replacement for #DerivedFrom, and 52 clauses were unread so the type hierarchy was invisible. DELIVERED: `TypeDef.specializes`, a `parse_specializes` helper called at all six def sites via an extracted `type_def_tail` (the extraction removes duplication this change itself introduced), and registry resolution of the target through the existing `check_type_ref`. ALSO FIXED, exposed by the positive control (issue103): the package's own declarations were absent from the validation scope, so a same-package supertype reported unresolved. VERIFY, both polarities measured: undeclared supertype FAILS with a semantic diagnostic; declared same-package supertype PASSES; no clause PASSES; real repo + .engine stay clean; `parser-coverage` no longer reports ColonGt. ALSO corrected the metric itself — capturing `:>` moved 52 records from ColonGt to LBrace WITHOUT changing the total, revealing that it counted skip_item INVOCATIONS rather than unread statements; `{` and `;` leads are no longer recorded, so the figure fell 165 -> 74 and now means what its name says. clippy clean; 161 tests; validate + all 27 guards + check-engine green."; }
