        verification serveAgentBridgeDoD : Test { :>> id = "a1c70094-0094-4394-9394-516273840394"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "D0094 m3 (the agent-bridge): UI actions ('critique this process/test/decision', 'investigate a finding', 'draft a report') spawn Claude Code headless (`claude -p --output-format stream-json --include-partial-messages`, scoped tools, setting_sources=project to load CLAUDE.md, resumable session), STREAMING the agent's work to the UI over SSE (not polling). AUTH: pipe to the LOCALLY-AUTHENTICATED `claude` CLI (the user's subscription/ENTERPRISE session); the server MUST NOT set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY (it overrides the subscription + forces pricier API-rate billing) — D0094. The agent runs under the engine's EXISTING discipline (skills + write API + guards + >=Medium human-disposition); NO new permission policy; the agent NEVER auto-commits (commits/acceptance stay the human's gate, D0016); per-action cost/turn CAP + a concurrency limit; localhost-only. The UI exposes OBVIOUS review/override hooks (see the work, accept/finding/override via apply-review, re-run). Degrades gracefully if the `claude` CLI is absent. VERIFY: a UI 'critique' streams a real headless-agent critique into the console; the result lands as a tracked critique via the write path; cost is metered + capped; no auto-commit; clippy + cargo test + guard all green."; }
