        // ── Field/retro-finding resolvers (2026-07-14, keel-serve dogfood + retro audit) — tracked, not yet done. ──
        action fixServeOrientPerf; // issue063: cut orient's git-subprocess storm (criterion-drift) that spikes serve first-load to 16-23s.
        verification fixServeOrientPerfDoD : Test { :>> id = "a1c70170-0170-4170-9170-516273840170"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Resolves issue063 (field-discovered via keel serve). ROOT (measured, corrected from 'hundreds'): orient spawns 19 git processes — batched cat-file (2) + a per-task fallback (git_criterion_at: git ls-tree + N git show) firing for ~5 done tasks whose dep DoD moved files; the fallback = ~15 avoidable spawns whose Windows CreateProcess/Defender tail amplifies to the intermittent 16-23s spike. FIX (perf-only, orient output UNCHANGED = not a view-meaning change, so EXECUTE not CHANGE): (a) git_criterion_at now does ONE `git grep -h -F` for the DoD's single-line declaration at the commit instead of ls-tree + N shows (extraction identical -> byte-identical orient); (b) the serve `cached` compute runs via tokio::task::block_in_place so a slow cold compute never STARVES the multi-thread runtime's worker. VERIFIED: orient JSON byte-identical before/after (diff clean); git spawns 19->9; A/B n=40 each (CLI cold): median 1211->847ms, p95 1769->1077ms, max 1820->1145ms (whole distribution down ~35%); NEW n=100: median 841, p99 1154, MAX 1154ms, 0 spikes >3s; live serve concurrency: a /api/item returned 0.29s WHILE orient computed 1.03s (no worker starvation). HONEST LIMIT: the 16-23s spikes are too rare (~1/50, external) to A/B statistically — the win is the measured distribution shift + halved spawn count (fewer spike opportunities), not a proof the spike rate dropped. clippy + cargo test (80) + keel validate + guard green."; }
        part fixServeOrientPerfDoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "58c60839-4adc-4460-ac1f-4213945a6ca4"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "50238fc"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-07-14"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeOpus"; }

        action surfaceDodDescription; // issue064: the console shows action/ready items as empty (+ a NextWork contains-edge), hiding the DoD procedureText.
        verification surfaceDodDescriptionDoD : Test { :>> id = "a1c70171-0171-4171-9171-516273840171"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Resolves issue064 (field-discovered via keel serve). An action task (e.g. proveProcessDeployment) genuinely has no authored attrs — correct — but its description lives in the verify-linked <task>DoD Test's procedureText, which the element view never surfaces; it shows the low-value structural `contains` edge from the NextWork action-def container instead, so a well-specified task LOOKS empty. FIX: the element/console view resolves <task>DoD (the verify-linked Test) and presents its procedureText (+ method) as the task's description. VERIFY: viewing a ready action in the console/element view shows its DoD criterion text; clippy + cargo test + keel validate + guard green."; }
