        action osAdaptiveCommandGuidance; // issue065: AI shell guidance is Windows-hardcoded + the downstream keel-init template ships NO OS guidance.
        verification osAdaptiveCommandGuidanceDoD : Test { :>> id = "a1c70172-0172-4172-9172-516273840172"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "Resolves issue065 (retro finding; generalizes issue013). CLAUDE.md Sec 6 is hardcoded to Windows/PowerShell/miniforge, and the shipped downstream template (keel-cli/assets/claude-md-template.md) has NO OS/env section — so future AI (here when a shell tool glitches; downstream on macOS/Linux) makes avoidable shell-mismatch mistakes. FIX: state the PRINCIPLE (detect + adapt to the host OS/shell; use OS-appropriate command forms; verify the shell before assuming syntax) in the operating guidance, keeping the Windows specifics as this repo's concrete instance; add a short OS/shell section to the downstream template so init'd projects on any OS inherit it. Record a lightweight convention Decision if it rises to one. VERIFY: CLAUDE.md Sec 6 states the OS-adaptive principle; the template carries an OS/shell section; doc-sync; keel validate + guard green."; }
