        action jvmRetirementSpike; // issue066: RESEARCH SPIKE — scope whether the Rust validator can cover .engine SysML semantics to retire the JVM kernel entirely.
        verification jvmRetirementSpikeDoD : Test { :>> id = "a1c70173-0173-4173-9173-516273840173"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "Resolves issue066 (architecture opportunity from the D0048 review). D0048 kept the JVM kernel as the .engine schema/workflow/instance SysML oracle (deep semantics the Rust validator does not cover); so engine commits still need conda + a ~20s JVM start and inherit an environment-fragile dependency. This is a WorkKind::research SPIKE (chartered to issue066 or a proposed Decision, per researchSpikeCharterRule/D0111): enumerate EXACTLY which checks the kernel validators (validate_schema/workflows/instances) perform that Rust does not, assess the cost/feasibility of replicating them in Rust, and produce a design artifact + a PROPOSED Decision on whether to retire the kernel entirely (with a migration path if yes). Implementation is a follow-on program gated on human acceptance. VERIFY: a design artifact enumerating the semantic gap + a recorded proposed Decision; keel validate + guard green."; }
