        verification engineRefResolverDoD : Test { :>> id = "a1c70174-0174-4174-9174-516273840174"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Resolves issue067 + delivers D0112 phase 2. DELIVERED: `keel check-engine` (lib::validate_engine_instances) registers ALL .engine packages then runs the SAME PackageRegistry::validate used for .tracking against the .engine INSTANCE files (decisions/processes/views + skills-registry + tracking-template; schema/workflow defs registered-not-validated) — KERNEL-FREE. Catches the `unresolved` class: unresolved type references + unknown import namespaces (the two the kernel's error-keyword set flags). Cross-file refs resolve (Rust registers all first — the advantage over the per-file kernel, issue021/024). WIRED as the SKIP_VALIDATE-proof backstop: added to ci.yml (Rust-only CI now runs keel validate + guard + check-engine, so a hook-skipped commit is still caught) AND to .githooks/pre-commit (local, kernel-free). SCOPE HONESTY: name/type EXISTENCE, NOT full type-conformance/specialization (that residual stays the kernel's, D0112 phase 3 — the kernel is not removed). VERIFIED: check-engine clean on the live repo (0 false positives); a synthetic broken probe flagged BOTH `unknown import namespace` + `unresolved type reference`; is_engine_instance_file unit test; clippy --workspace --all-targets + cargo test (82) + keel validate + guard green; doc-sync CLAUDE.md §5. Governed by D0112 (#ProspectiveChange)."; }
