        action dcMachineScopeRestatement;
        verification dcMachineScopeRestatementDoD : Test { :>> id = "e93b1d57-4c82-40a6-b715-8f2e06da3947"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "Resolves issue137. D0115 clause 1 says 'the viewer is single-user + unauthenticated', which is inconsistent with shipped behaviour: D0108/D0129 already give one BOUND ACTOR PER MACHINE with several machines collaborating through git. DO: author a Decision superseding that clause, restating the boundary as 'one bound actor per machine; collaboration by git; the console is local-only and unauthenticated', and sweep every claim derived from the old phrase - requirements, viewpoint concerns, docs - fixing each in the same commit. Human acceptance required: this is a scope statement in an accepted Decision, not a wording nit. VERIFY: no live artifact asserts single-user of the ENGINE; the console's local-only scope is stated where a reader meets it; the superseding Decision carries its acceptance."; }
