        action dcConsoleBuildStamp;
        verification dcConsoleBuildStampDoD : Test { :>> id = "2f60d84b-9c17-4e53-8a26-71be05fc3d92"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Resolves issue153. The console build id is a hash of the page's own bytes, substituted into the HTML BY THE SERVER so `build <id>` renders with no JavaScript - verified live: `Technical smooth sailing - build 87f94652` is present in the raw response and the __KEEL_BUILD__ placeholder count is zero. Exposed as `consoleBuild` on /api/version, distinct from apiVersion because the API contract holds steady across page changes. The page compares its embedded id with the server's on every SSE hello and every 30s and reloads when they differ, so a tab open across a restart removes itself instead of running dead logic. STATED LIMIT: a page already stale when this shipped has no such check and needs one manual reload."; }
