        action dcDeckForkOptions;
        verification dcDeckForkOptionsDoD : Test { :>> id = "b8c9f12c-9e23-4ba0-ab48-ea65b8154505"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Resolves issue223. The deck rendered fork Decision d0192 (which enumerates OPTION A / OPTION B and states that accepting means choosing ONE) as a single bare Sign button; wweatherholtz tapped it and the gesture could not bind - solicited and wasted, the D0054 friction class. DO: the deck detects OPTION-enumerating proposed decisions (fork_options: two or more 'OPTION X (label)' captures) and renders one sign button per option; the chosen option is stamped into the note on BOTH transports (local API and remote inbox row), so the recorded acceptance carries the choice; tapping a different option switches rather than clears. VERIFY: unit test pins the D0192 text shape; the regenerated deck shows 'Sign A - amend the requirement' and 'Sign B - close the path' with data-opt attributes; emitted JS still parses; full suite and clippy green."; }
