        verification dcConfirmationRecordDelegationDoD : Test { :>> id = "dbe448f9-cc57-4acb-a085-6839c35b232b"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Resolves issue224 (srK06a completeness critique). The D0192 OPTION A delegation is declared and substance-checked for decisionAcceptance only, but the SAME practice records DoD confirmation flips (sprint 420's own dcHumanChannelDelegationRuleDoD flip is the live example) with no [confirmationRecord] policy class and no quote demand - the asymmetry D0192 closed for acceptances, one level down. DO: design where a delegated confirmation flip's quote LIVES (a DoD result has no note field - the evidence shape differs from acceptance events, so this is design, not a copy of the acceptance check), declare the class in attestation-policy.toml, extend or add the substance rule. VERIFY: a delegated confirmation flip recorded without its quote fails the guard; the policy contract names every practiced delegation class."; }
