        verification dcRulesUnderKeystoneDoD : Test { :>> id = "4a794bb4-45bf-43f7-a367-1be47d1d189c"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Resolves issue236 (D0208 control evaluation, HIGH). The control-eval proved an agent could downgrade a blocking ElementRule to a warning in .engine/rules/ and NO guard fired - process-change's is_process_def did not cover the rules directory, so the enforcement DEFINITIONS were editable by the monitored without a signed decision (the AI-safety panel's self-modification gap, made concrete). DO: is_process_def includes .engine/rules/*.sysml so any rule edit requires a co-committed #ProspectiveChange/#SafetyChange Decision - a human-signed act. VERIFY: a committed rule severity-flip turns process-change RED (probed live in the throwaway worktree: was PASS scanned-0, now FAIL scanned-1); the real tree's rule edits this sprint ride a marked decision."; }
        part dcRulesUnderKeystoneDoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "fbdc8fad-df74-4884-b2e2-532a69516443"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "e14fbfbccab54785510fd0e2a74eabefc59347af"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-24"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeFable5"; }
        action dcDanglingResultAtGate;
        verification dcDanglingResultAtGateDoD : Test { :>> id = "54bf0295-1933-4c6a-af4f-818310a4d9da"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "Resolves issue237 (D0208 control eval, LOW). A free-floating TestResult whose judgedAgainst SHA does not resolve passes validate+guard: the commit gate does not check SHA resolvability. The TRACKED case is covered - orient invalidEvidence flags a task whose evidence SHA dangles, and CI audit-history re-derives verdicts - so an UNREFERENCED garbage-SHA result is inert (computes nothing). DO: decide whether the commit gate should reject a dangling judgedAgainst at write time, or whether orient+audit-history coverage of the tracked case suffices; if the latter, this is accept-risk with the reason recorded. VERIFY: either a guard flags a dangling-SHA result, or the disposition records why the existing tracked-case coverage is sufficient."; }
