        action dcWhichProject;
        verification dcWhichProjectDoD : Test { :>> id = "f1d2266f-4619-4b8b-8e3e-2be678256fb9"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Resolves issue268 (D0233), reported by the author while using the console. INVESTIGATED FIRST and the finding changed the answer: the server side of their suggested feature already existed - /api/projects discovers sibling keel projects and names the active one, POST /api/project switches and refuses a non-project - and NOTHING RENDERED EITHER, so a capability shipped with no surface. DO: the startup banner prints the ROOT before anything else; the page TITLE becomes project-dot-keel, substituted server-side so the browser TAB is right on first paint and right even if the page JavaScript never runs; the header carries a project badge whose tooltip is the full root, beside a switcher populated from /api/projects that POSTs to /api/project and reloads, hidden when only one project is reachable; a display_path helper strips the Windows verbatim prefix at every display site. VERIFY AGAINST A RUNNING SERVER, not by reading: the banner names the root; the title reads sysmlv2-ai-toolkit dot keel; a POST switch flips it to Penumbra dot keel; C:/Windows is REFUSED with the active project unchanged and the reason reported; switching back restores it; nine reachable projects are discovered so the switcher is populated."; }
