        verification dcWorkspaceSurfaceIsOwnedDoD : Test { :>> id = "9c18787c-8fe3-4c38-9223-501235b1f557"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Resolves issue276. In a workspace the repo-root enforcement surface belongs to no project, so the keystone lock can never fire on it: verified by replacing the single hook that gates every project with exit 0, staged alone with no Decision - gate --workspace reported 2 projects gated clean, exit 0, printing a line that NAMES the unowned file and passing anyway. Same for the root workflows directory. Also verified: staging the deletion of an entire project, 445 paths, passes the gate. DO: gate_cmd applies the keystone check to unowned staged paths against the repo root and EXITS NON-ZERO; a staged deletion of any engine path, owned or not, is a keystone event. VERIFY: the exit-0 hook replacement is BLOCKED; deleting a project is BLOCKED; a legitimate signed change still passes."; }
        // RAN: see sprint473_lockCoverage RAN receipt: 11 suites 0 failures; unsigned exit-0 hook swap BLOCKED exit 1 (was exit 0 with 2 projects gated clean); project deletion 447 paths BLOCKED 402 keystone events (was silent); signed change PASSES; unsigned rule weakening FAILS at three depths - repo root, inside the project, and deeper (one directory down previously PASSED); signed weakening PASSES; single-project parity measured - PASS, zero qualified keys, project_prefixes == empty
