        verification dcAdherenceIsWorkspaceAwareDoD : Test { :>> id = "9f84b605-2ce1-4d04-8342-9fbbbbe44ebc"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Resolves issue277. The keystone added-file exemption from issue272 was justified by naming audit-adherence as the compensating control, and audit-adherence is BLIND in a multi-project repo: its pathspecs are repo-root-relative, which match nothing when projects live one directory down. Verified with an identical unsigned rule weakening - single-project FAIL exit 1; workspace PASS exit 0, both from the root and from inside the project. So one control was weakened while citing another that does not work in the arrangement the same Decision introduced. DO: iterate the discovered project set in the adherence signature and process-set reads, prefixing each pathspec with the project label, and fail loudly when a discovered project yields zero rule files; until that lands, gate the added-file exemption on a single-project repo. VERIFY: the unsigned weakening FAILS in a workspace at every depth; single-project behaviour unchanged."; }
