        action dcWorkspaceIsWireable;
        verification dcWorkspaceIsWireableDoD : Test { :>> id = "238418b0-393a-4575-bc76-4e6660a42f4b"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Resolves issue278. A freshly created workspace is COMPLETELY ungated and nothing scaffolds the wiring: init writes hooks per project and only sets core.hooksPath when the target itself holds a git directory, so creating two projects in one repo leaves no repo-root hook and no hooksPath - verified, a commit then ran with zero pre-commit lines. Worse, the refusal message added in the same change advises keel hook pre-commit, which is not a hook event and exits 0 silently: anyone wiring it installs a gate that passes while checking nothing, reintroducing issue269 inside its own fix. DO: when init's target is not the repo root, write or merge the repo-root hook calling gate --workspace, set core.hooksPath, and print workspace-correct next steps; change the advice string to name a command that gates. VERIFY: a two-project workspace created only with documented commands is gated; the advice string names a command that actually gates."; }
