        action dcLandGatesBeforeThePush;
        verification dcLandGatesBeforeThePushDoD : Test { :>> id = "c18ddc3e-96ae-4bd0-8c0f-08279d8e02d3"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Resolves issue280. D0234 claims land gates every project before a push. It does not: cmd_land pushes first and only reaches the gate after a REJECTION and merge, so on the success path nothing is gated. Verified with a bare remote - a project with a broken tracking file, committed with the skip flag, then land from a different project: landed, exit 0, and the broken file is in the remote. cmd_sync does gate unconditionally; only land is holed, and the Decision asserts a property it lacks. DO: gate before the first push. VERIFY: land REFUSES with a broken project anywhere in the workspace; a clean workspace still lands; the Decision text is corrected."; }
