        verification dcOwnerOfMatchesOnWindowsDoD : Test { :>> id = "45839853-5747-4947-8647-c4cdb0a301de"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Resolves issue284. keel projects advertises which project you are in and it never works on this platform: the command canonicalizes the working directory, which on Windows yields the extended-length prefix with backslashes, while discovery takes the root from git in forward-slash form, so the prefix comparison never matches. Verified: from inside a project no marker is printed and the JSON reports current false for every project, including in all eight real repos. Two panelists found it independently. The unit test passes only because it builds the structure by hand from POSIX literals, never through discovery. DO: normalise both sides once inside discovery, through the display-path helper D0233 already added. VERIFY: a test that goes through discovery on the real tree and asserts the owning project of the working directory is found."; }
