        action dcWorkspace;
        verification dcWorkspaceDoD : Test { :>> id = "d54a993d-23e5-44f7-a9c2-a5421e9d4ae6"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Resolves issue270 (D0234). The author wants one repo for several small projects and expects it to recur. BUILT AND RAN the arrangement rather than reasoning about it: three things already worked (root resolution walks up, drift is file-scoped per project, the write lock is per model root) and FOUR broke - decision numbering collides at d0001, the channel cannot tell two projects apart because its marker and GitHub lookup are repo-scoped, git allows ONE core.hooksPath so at most one project is gated, and land gates one root while pushing the whole repo. DO: a WORKSPACE is a git repo holding one or more projects, DISCOVERED as a directory with both .engine and .tracking by a depth-bounded walk; keel projects reports them; keel gate --workspace gates every project a commit touches and NAMES the skipped ones; the scaffolded pre-commit calls it when its own directory is not a project; sync and land gate EVERY project before pushing; validate REFUSES a non-project; the channel qualifies an id as alpha/d0001 only when the repo holds several, split in the binary so a human acceptance lands in the right tree. VERIFY LIVE: two projects in one repo with ONE repo-root hook gate a commit across both; a broken project BLOCKS the commit and the report names the project it skipped; a single-project repo is byte-identical - the qualification rule returns d0231 unchanged, and this repo reports exactly one project."; }
